    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nIs there a way that we can display file info e.g., size, last edit time etc when navigating the file system. This is the only feature I miss after migrating from `oil.nvim`. \r\n\r\nNow I have to open terminal and `ll` just to find out the size of the files that I have generated. \r\n\r\nThanks for your consideration!",
    "closed_at": "2025-01-10T10:17:32Z",
