            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n'mini.files' implements the flexible concept of [content prefix](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-files.txt#L635-L642), which by default shows only highlighted icon. It can be adjusted however user wants.\r\n\r\nHere is an [example of how to adjust it](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-files.txt#L431-L440). And here is an example of how to add file size in prefix:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal format_size = function(size)\r\n  if size == nil then return end\r\n  if size < 1024 then\r\n    return string.format('%3dB', size)\r\n  elseif size < 1048576 then\r\n    return string.format('%3.0fK', size / 1024)\r\n  else\r\n    return string.format('%3.0fM', size / 1048576)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\nlocal my_prefix = function(fs_entry)\r\n  local prefix, hl = MiniFiles.default_prefix(fs_entry)\r\n  local fs_stat = vim.loop.fs_stat(fs_entry.path) or {}\r\n  return format_size(fs_stat.size) .. ' ' .. prefix, hl\r\nend\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup({ content = { prefix = my_prefix } })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere are two downsides here:\r\n- It will be computed in blocking way for every item in the directory when entering it, which might introduce small lags for complex prefixes. This might change in the future after support for Neovim 0.9 version is dropped (not very soon, I think, though).\r\n- File info will be highlighted in the same way as icon, but highlighting whole prefix in the same way is something that won't change, I am afraid.",
